"{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.5871/bacad/9780197262856.003.0003\",\n  \"title\": \"From the dialects of Old Indo-Aryan to Proto-Indo-Aryan and Proto-Iranian\",\n  \"authors\": \"Asko Parpola\",\n  \"abstract\": \"<p>The Aryan or Indo-Iranian languages are divided into two basic groups, Indo-Aryan (i.e. languages nowadays mainly spoken in India in its pre-1947 sense of South Asia) and Iranian (i.e. languages nowadays mainly spoken in Iran, also rather in the historical sense of the Persian Empire, which extended to Central Asia and the Indus Valley). This chapter discusses how this dialectal split goes back to the very emergence of Proto-Aryan from Late Proto-Indo-European, far from India and Iran.</p>\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.5871/bacad/9780197262856.003.0003\",\n  \"published_date\": \"2003-01-23T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.5871/bacad/9780197262856.003.0003\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"book-chapter\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 2,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'British Academy', 'container_title': 'Indo-Iranian Languages and Peoples', 'volume': '', 'issue': '', 'page': '', 'issn': [], 'isbn': ['9780197262856', '9780191753961'], 'crossref_type': 'book-chapter', 'member': '3895', 'prefix': '10.5871'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.31862/2500-2953-2025-4-9-26\",\n  \"title\": \"Indo-Aryan infinitives in bahuvrīhi compounds: from Old Indo-Aryan to Middle Indo-Aryan languages\",\n  \"authors\": \"S. Kamadanova\",\n  \"abstract\": \"\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.31862/2500-2953-2025-4-9-26\",\n  \"published_date\": \"2025-01-01T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"https://rhema-journal.com/Rema_2025_4_Kamadanova.pdf\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.31862/2500-2953-2025-4-9-26\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"journal-article\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 0,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'Federal State Budgetary Educational Institution of Higher Education 束Moscow Pedagogical State University損 (MPGU)', 'container_title': 'Rhema', 'volume': '4', 'issue': '', 'page': '', 'issn': ['2500-2953'], 'isbn': [], 'crossref_type': 'journal-article', 'member': '17119', 'prefix': '10.31862'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.1075/sl.36.4.01kul\",\n  \"title\": \"Vedic preverbs as markers of valency-changing derivations\",\n  \"authors\": \"Leonid Kulikov\",\n  \"abstract\": \"<jats:p>The present paper offers an analysis of the transitivizing and intransitivizing preverbs (semi-bound verbal prefixes) in Vedic Sanskrit. I will argue that the (in)transitivizing force of these morphemes is weak: the passivization test shows that transitivizing preverbs only exceptionally make fundamentally intransitive verbs true transitives, whilst the only intransitivizing preverb <jats:italic>ví</jats:italic> has but a rather limited valency-changing capacity.</jats:p>\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.1075/sl.36.4.01kul\",\n  \"published_date\": \"2012-12-31T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1075/sl.36.4.01kul\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"journal-article\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 8,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'John Benjamins Publishing Company', 'container_title': 'Studies in Language', 'volume': '36', 'issue': '4', 'page': '721-746', 'issn': ['0378-4177', '1569-9978'], 'isbn': [], 'crossref_type': 'journal-article', 'member': '1757', 'prefix': '10.1075'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.1163/9789401207973_002\",\n  \"title\": \"Vedic -ya-formations: preliminaries\",\n  \"authors\": \"Leonid Kulikov\",\n  \"abstract\": \"\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.1163/9789401207973_002\",\n  \"published_date\": \"2012-01-01T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1163/9789401207973_002\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"book-chapter\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 0,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'BRILL', 'container_title': 'The Vedic -&lt;i&gt;ya&lt;/i&gt;-presents', 'volume': '', 'issue': '', 'page': '1-16', 'issn': [], 'isbn': ['9789401207973', '9789042035225'], 'crossref_type': 'book-chapter', 'member': '374', 'prefix': '10.1163'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.1515/jsall-2016-0005\",\n  \"title\": \"Leonid Kulikov: The Vedic -ya-presents: Passives and intransitivity in Old Indo-Aryan\",\n  \"authors\": \"Martin Kümmel\",\n  \"abstract\": \"\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.1515/jsall-2016-0005\",\n  \"published_date\": \"2016-03-01T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1515/jsall-2016-0005\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"journal-article\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 0,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'Walter de Gruyter GmbH', 'container_title': 'Journal of South Asian Languages and Linguistics', 'volume': '3', 'issue': '1', 'page': '131-132', 'issn': ['2196-0771', '2196-078X'], 'isbn': [], 'crossref_type': 'journal-article', 'member': '374', 'prefix': '10.1515'}\"\n}"
